  "workarounds": [
    {
      "followup": "EF-71",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "col() writes the hex beside each paletteId: 1.4.1 paints the running heads, the cover and the heading designs from the hex (gotcha palette-skips-designs)"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-05",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the H1 breakBefore is restated because a headings object drops it"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-90",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the cover drawing is an image and reserves nothing; minHeight (SINK, 34 lines of 13 pt) holds the letter at 177.9 mm, where without it the letter starts 55 mm from the top, over the drawing"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-18",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the cover's frame is drawn from the cover style's header (pages: 'opener'): as a design element it reached 242 mm down the page, more than the column holds, and the opener's whole reservation was dropped, setting the letter under the title"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-34",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "the Kind merges and the order sheet's totals go through mergeCells, which keeps the covered cells in the grid marked hiddenBy"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-65",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "in the 75 mm columns Knuth–Plass stretched the spaces of 13 of the 27 justified lines past maxWordSpacing (worst 2.13 times a normal space); the letter and the trial notes were reworded until the loosest line stretched them 1.33 times"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-79",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "with 13 lines of trial notes, closing-page balancing put a blank grid line above From Our Trial Garden (196.3 mm against 191.7 mm for column 2); the notes are fitted to 14 lines, so both columns open level under the list"
    },
    {
      "followup": "EF-151",
      "package": "postext",
      "note": "table cells are not parsed for maths and do not unescape \\$: a cell written '\\$4.50' prints the backslash, so the prices and the postage line write $ bare (gotcha cell-dollar-backslash)"
    }
  ],
